    "scope": "The model uses the signed exact way 82650638 and Q1166032 frame at [60.79475474, 46.098499985], heading −0.435207816096 radians. The 57.325 m regulator spans the two mapped shoulders. The North Aral reservoir lies on the northeast side and the modeled regulator drains southwest into the native outlet. The 12,759.79 m sampled KNA-22 crest trace is distinct from the 13,034 m retained source length. Seven centerline probes across the regulator fall inside the authored deck. All 27 native road records remain in the fixture and the placement carries no road replacement.",
    "notes": "Crest, sill and tailwater grades are approximate at 64 m terrain resolution. Minor seams remain where the low banks meet the regional terrain. The operating level and unpictured machinery are illustrative. The full live PMTiles/terrain stream and physical-device timings were outside this local fixture review."
